# Every slot of graphicsdict the machinery reaches by a dotted name, and
# which of the two kinds it is. check-callout-bracket.sh holds the tree
# to this register, so a slot added later cannot quietly become a third
# kind: it is one or the other, and saying which is part of adding it.
#
#   bracketed  something a procedure parks across a call out to program
#              code and reads back afterwards. It must be named in a key
#              array handed to .callout, so that a callback re-entering
#              the machinery cannot cost the caller what it parked.
#
#   lifetime   state of the render itself, which no callback is mid-use
#              of: it means the same thing before a callback and after,
#              and putting the outgoing value back would undo work the
#              callback was called to do.
#
# The distinction is not about how long the value lives but about who is
# mid-use of it. A cache the whole render shares is lifetime; a value one
# procedure left in a slot because the operand stack belongs to the
# callback is bracketed.

bracketed /.csspace
bracketed /.csstash
bracketed /.convdepth
bracketed /.inglyph
bracketed /.t3want
bracketed /.t3cap
bracketed /.tsproc
bracketed /.tsop
bracketed /.tsd
bracketed /.ssd0
bracketed /.ssrec
bracketed /.ctrec
bracketed /.ctop
bracketed /.csrec

lifetime /.formcache
lifetime /.formlast
lifetime /.exactpagedims
lifetime /.rasterband
lifetime /.devrequest
lifetime /.devpending
lifetime /.pagedevice
lifetime /.outputdevice
